(Page 1 - Computer Networks) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
0 -28 Td
(A computer network is two or more computing devices joined together) Tj
(to exchange data and share resources. The devices may be wired with) Tj
(copper or fibre, or joined wirelessly over radio. A protocol is an) Tj
(agreed set of rules that lets two devices understand each other.) Tj
(The TCP/IP model has four layers. Each layer adds a service for the) Tj
(layer above it and hides how the lower layers work. A packet created) Tj
(at the application layer travels down the stack, crosses the network,) Tj
(and is rebuilt on the far side.) Tj
(The TCP handshake is a three-step exchange. The client sends SYN, the) Tj
(server replies SYN-ACK, and the client answers with ACK. Only after) Tj
(this sequence is the connection established. If any step is lost the) Tj
(handshake restarts, which is why a failed handshake costs time.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
