/F1 16 Tf
72 720 Td
(Page 2 - Switching and Addressing) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
0 -28 Td
(An Ethernet switch forwards frames using a MAC address table. Each) Tj
(port learns which MAC address sits behind it by watching the source) Tj
(address of arriving frames. A frame for an unknown address is flooded) Tj
(to every port except the one it arrived on.) Tj
(IP addressing is hierarchical. A router strips the network portion of) Tj
(the destination address and forwards the packet to the next hop. The) Tj
(Time to Live field decreases by one at every router, preventing loops.) Tj
(Subnet masks decide where the network number ends and the host number) Tj
(begins. A /24 mask reserves the final octet for hosts, giving 254) Tj
(usable addresses once the network and broadcast addresses are removed.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
