(Page 3 - Congestion and Reliability) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
0 -28 Td
(Congestion control has two main goals: keep the network efficient and) Tj
(keep any one sender from flooding the links it shares. The four phases) Tj
(of TCP congestion control are slow start, congestion avoidance, fast) Tj
(retransmit and fast recovery.) Tj
(Slow start doubles the sending window on every round trip until a) Tj
(packet is lost. Congestion avoidance then grows the window by one) Tj
(segment per round trip, which is far gentler. Fast retransmit sends) Tj
(the missing segment immediately after three duplicate ACKs, without) Tj
(waiting for a timeout.) Tj
(Retransmission timers must balance two failure modes. A timer set too) Tj
(low triggers needless resends and wastes bandwidth. A timer set too) Tj
(high leaves a gap in the connection. A dynamic estimate from measured) Tj
(round-trip times keeps the timer in between.) Tj
ET
endstream
